l and Molecular Engineering\nEngineering Science\nGraduate Programs\nChemical and Molecular Engineering\nMaterials Science and Engineering\nStudents\nOpportunities\nStudent Spotlights\nSeminar and Student Events\nStudent Resources\nForms\nFaculty\nOverview\nPostdocs and Research Scientists\nNS Adjunct Faculty\nFaculty Resources\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nCenters and Institutes\nConnect\nDirections\nMentor Connect\nAlumni Spotlight\nNews\nGiving\nWays to Give\nDonors\nMaterials Science and Chemical Engineering\nAcademics\nGraduate Program\nGraduate Program in Materials Science and Engineering\nRequest Information\nMaterials Science and Engineering PhD & MS\nAdvance your career through Stony Brook University\u2019s STEM-designated MS and PhD programs\nin Materials Science and Engineering. Our graduate programs prepare students to develop\ninnovative solutions for critical challenges in energy storage, semiconductors, nanotechnology,\nbiomaterials, advanced manufacturing, coatings, and sustainable materials through\ninterdisciplinary research and collaboration.\nStudents work alongside internationally recognized faculty, conduct research using\nstate-of-the-art facilities, and collaborate with leading research partners including\nBrookhaven National Laboratory and the Garcia Polymer Center. Through advanced coursework,\nhands-on research experiences, and interdisciplinary training, students gain the technical\nexpertise needed for careers in industry, academia, research institutions, and government\nlaboratories.\nCareer Outcomes\nThe U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics projects 7% growth in materials engineering jobs\nbetween 2023 and 2033. Nearly 95% of Stony Brook graduates are employed or continue their education through\nadvanced study. Stony Brook graduates are prepared for impactful careers across a wide range of technology-driven\nindustries.\nGraduates pursue careers in:\nResearch & Development\nMaterials Engineering & Product Development\nSemiconductors & Electronics\nAerospace & Advanced Manufacturing\nEnergy & Sustainability\nBiomedical Technologies\nNational Laboratories\nAcademia & Industry Leadership\nComplete the form to learn more about admissions, funding, research opportunities,\nand upcoming events in Stony Brook University\u2019s Chemical & Molecular Engineering graduate\nprograms.\nFor queries, please contact ESMandCME_GradAdmissions@stonybrook.edu\nRequest For Information\nLoading...\nMaterials Science and Chemical Engineering\n314 Engineering Building | Stony Brook University\nPHONE: 631-632-4986 | EMAIL: msce_office@stonybrook.edu\nPrivacy Policy\nReporting Discrimination\nSexual Misconduct\nAccessibility Barrier\n\u00a9 2026 Stony Brook University\n\u00a9", "links": [["", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/"], ["College of Engineering and Applied Sciences", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/ceas/"], ["Materials Science and Chemical Engineering", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng//index.html"], ["", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/index.html"], ["About", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/about/index.html"], ["Chair\u2019s Message and Fast Facts", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/about/chairs_message_and_fast_facts.html"], ["Administration and Staff", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/about/administration_and_staff.html"], ["Executive Committee Members", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/about/executive-committee-members.html"], ["Academics", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/index.html"], ["Overview", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/overview.html"], ["Undergraduate Programs", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/undergraduate-programs/index.html"], ["Chemical and Molecular Engineering", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/undergraduate-programs/undergraduate-program-in-chemical-and-molecular-engineering/index.html"], ["Engineering Science", "https://www.stonybrook.edu/matsci-chemeng/academics/u